id: pm-rl-od32
title: "Durable loop continuation: idempotent resume, controller lease, cancellation drills"
description: "Make the persisted recursive loop durable and crash-safe. pm rl loop run becomes idempotent: re-running after a crash at ANY phase (collect, train, evaluate, promote) never double-counts the sample budget, never re-promotes, and never loses an artifact; every partially persisted generation is completed from its persisted evidence. Add pm rl loop status <id> (read-only reconstruction) and pm rl loop resume <id> (resume from the persisted programme). Two controllers racing to launch the same loop produce exactly one job: the launch is guarded by the pm SDK's own primitives — an owner-bound claim on the loop seed plus the SDK workspace lock (acquireLock), with dead-holder takeover — never an invented lock file; proven by a real two-process test. SIGINT/SIGTERM/AbortSignal mid-phase leave consistent state that a resume completes to the identical uninterrupted result."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags[3]: durability,execution,recursive-training
created_at: "2026-10-05T04:32:30.577Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-11T06:57:13.948Z"
assignee: codex-agent
claim_principal: codex-agent
author: pi-glm
estimated_minutes: 960
acceptance_criteria: "pm rl loop run re-run after an injected failure at each phase boundary completes to the exact uninterrupted report, with one create per item in history and no duplicated metric events; pm rl loop status reports per-generation phase, consumed budget and terminal reason without mutating anything; pm rl loop resume completes an interrupted loop from the persisted seed configuration; two concurrent controller processes produce exactly one seed, one run per generation and one promotion, the loser failing with a stable contention error; a killed controller's lease is taken over promptly via dead-pid detection; AbortSignal/SIGTERM cancellation mid-phase stops at a phase boundary, leaves consistent state, and a subsequent resume completes the loop"
parent: pm-rl-apvf
comments[44]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-05T04:32:45.155Z",pi-glm,"Starting the durable-continuation slice on branch feat/durable-rsi-continuation. Design decisions recorded as I go: (1) launch mutual exclusion uses the pm SDK's own primitives — an owner-bound claim on the loop seed item plus the SDK workspace lock acquireLock per generation, with dead-pid takeover of an abandoned SDK lock record; no invented lock file. (2) resume reconstructs state from persisted items only: the deterministic bandit receipt is recomputed and verified against the stored training configuration, and missing metric-event suffixes are appended rather than re-collected. (3) pm rl loop run becomes idempotent end to end; the previous loop_already_started refusal is replaced by resume semantics, while a different configuration under the same loop id still conflicts through the content-addressed registration identity."
  "2026-10-05T05:04:20.384Z",codex-sol,"Resumed the interrupted implementation with codex-sol. Existing loop and calibration-head work is preserved; typecheck passes. Next verify lease safety, replay identities and existing regressions, then commit the implementation before adding crash, process-contention and cancellation proofs. Feature items remain open until orchestrator verification."
  "2026-10-05T05:21:48.906Z",codex-sol,Crash-phase replay and OS-process contention/cancellation proofs now run against real SDK projects. SIGKILL dead-controller takeover plus SIGINT and SIGTERM resumes pass. Cross-worktree audit exposed duplicate seed create identities when registration preceded shared launch authority; acquisition now precedes all job artifact creation and uses SDK acquireLock plus an SDK Decision journal under shared Git metadata. Losing worktrees leave no duplicate job artifacts. Exact coverage is pending.
  "2026-10-05T05:56:17.039Z",codex-sol,"Verified collect/train/evaluate/promote replay, partial decision-note cancellation, actual CLI SIGINT/SIGTERM handlers, SIGKILL dead-controller recovery, real two-process launch exclusion, two Git worktree merge/replay, rejected-budget accounting and receipt corruption refusals. PM-linked durability test passed 14 tests; full coverage run passed 386 tests and exposed three controller failure branches. Added SDK lease failure and launch-journal/read failure drills for those branches; focused checks pass. No threshold or source exclusions changed."
  "2026-10-05T06:05:07.654Z",codex-sol,"Final npm run release:check passed 387/387 tests, zero skips and exact 100/100/100/100 statements/lines/branches/functions over all 23 authored source files including scripts. No ignores or lowered thresholds. Strict TypeScript, ESLint, zero jscpd clones, 200 documented declarations, publish attestation, identity audit, zero production vulnerabilities, pack dry run and changelog check passed. Final PM-linked node --test test/durable-loop.test.ts passed 15/15. Strict pm health passed. Items remain open for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-10-05T06:09:56.770Z",codex-sol,"Draft PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rl/pull/62 contains the verified continuation slice and full gate evidence. Authored TypeScript source matches the release-checked implementation commit a135cd0; documentation and packaged example are in 963506f. Claims released; feature and epic remain open."
  "2026-10-05T06:32:25.583Z",codex-sol,"Addressing PR #62 review findings 4181277126 and 4181277135: strengthen controller identity without timed takeover, add audited explicit resume takeover, canonicalize launch authority through real paths, and verify all-source release gates."
  "2026-10-05T06:37:34.744Z",codex-sol,"Implemented host/PID/birth-time identity checks with conservative ambiguity handling and no elapsed-time takeover. Explicit resume force takeover is audited before unlinking; matching live identities remain protected. Launch ownership now hashes canonical real paths. Regression tests cover real child PID reuse, live identity despite old timestamps, foreign-host refusal and CLI audited override, portable probe fallbacks, and an actual symlink alias. The host reserved-flag registry does not own --force-takeover."
  "2026-10-05T06:46:39.911Z",codex-sol,"PM-linked node --test test/durable-loop.test.ts passed 21/21 with zero failures or skips using an isolated snapshot and a 300-second timeout. Focused portable-probe and SDK lock-failure checks pass; typecheck, test build, docstrings and zero-duplication checks pass. npm run changelog:full regenerated the changelog with no new completed release entries. Strict pm health exits zero with two existing advisories tracked in follow-up pm-rl-9uz4. Full npm run release:check coverage is still running."
  "2026-10-05T06:59:08.202Z",codex-sol,"PR #62 findings 4181277126 and 4181277135 fixed in ce7c044. Final frozen-code npm run release:check exited 0: 393/393 tests, zero failures/skips, exact 100/100/100/100 statements/lines/branches/functions across all 23 sources, no coverage exclusions, 202 documented declarations, strict typecheck/lint, zero duplication, approved identities, publish attestation, zero production vulnerabilities, pack dry run and changelog check. PM-linked node --test test/durable-loop.test.ts passed 21/21; portable-probe and SDK recovery-failure focused checks also passed. npm run changelog:full regenerated the unchanged completed-release changelog. Strict pm health passes with existing advisories tracked in pm-rl-9uz4. Portable fallback limitations are documented; native macOS/Windows acceptance was not run. Item remains in_progress for orchestrator verification; no GitHub thread replies or merge."
  "2026-10-05T09:00:34.971Z",codex-sol,"Addressing re-review findings 4182097297 and 4182097312: require a verifiable own birth time before acquiring locks, publish enriched identity atomically under the recovery mutex, block forced takeover of live local holders with unavailable identity probes, and document platform precision limits. The pinned SDK acquireLock signature has no metadata parameter."
  "2026-10-05T09:08:15.951Z",codex-sol,"Focused re-review regressions passed 4/4: own-probe failure refuses before any acquisition even with force, unavailable live-holder probing and missing legacy identity prevent takeover, and identity publication changes the lock inode atomically while preserving the SDK token and excluding recovery during the raw-record window. Claim receipts reuse the captured own birth time. Tests inject the existing process probe IO seam and use real SDK locks and filesystem observations, without filesystem mocks. README and durable validation docs qualify macOS/BSD one-second PID reuse and require waiting for the unrelated process to exit before retrying."
  "2026-10-05T09:21:02.696Z",codex-sol,"Re-review findings 4182097297 and 4182097312 fixed in 872b980. Frozen-code npm run release:check exited 0: 396/396 tests, zero failures/skips, exact 100/100/100/100 statements/lines/branches/functions over all 23 sources, 203 documented declarations, no exclusions or lowered thresholds, strict typecheck/lint, zero duplication, identity/publish-attestation gates, zero production vulnerabilities, pack dry run and changelog check. pm test pm-rl-od32 --run --progress passed both linked commands: node --test test/durable-loop.test.ts (24/24) and the focused unavailable-own/live-local-PID/atomic-publication/ambiguous-local pattern (4/4). Probe failures are injected through the existing IO seam without filesystem mocks; atomic publication uses real SDK locks and inode/token observations. README documents platform-qualified reuse detection and waiting for an unrelated same-second process to exit. Strict pm health passes with the existing advisories already tracked in pm-rl-9uz4. Native macOS/Windows execution remains unverified. Claims will be released; item stays in_progress for orchestrator verification. No GitHub replies."
  "2026-10-05T09:32:06.759Z",codex-sol,"Verified review 4182506926: existing bandit candidates bypass collection batch validation. Require exact receipt event count, identities and rewards before replay accepts promoted or refused candidates; add lost, changed and duplicated collection evidence regressions."
  "2026-10-05T09:34:48.179Z",codex-sol,"The new terminal-evidence regression reproduced the original bug: loop status accepted a promoted candidate after its collection note was deleted. Added persisted SDK note deletion, rewriting and duplication cases for both promoted and refused candidates, with status and resume required to reject without altering candidate history. Exact event replay now checks the complete batch before candidate verdicts."
  "2026-10-05T09:36:00.199Z",codex-sol,"Focused regression PASS: node --test --test-name-pattern=\"terminal bandit candidates\" test/durable-loop.test.ts, also run via pm test pm-rl-od32 --run --progress --only-last. Twelve persisted corruption cases cover promoted/refused candidates, lost notes, rewards, duplicates, incomplete batches and changed example/action identities; status and resume reject each without candidate history changes. Typecheck, lint, zero duplication, 203 docstrings and build:test pass. Full release check pending."
  "2026-10-05T09:45:42.782Z",codex-sol,"Review 4182506926 fixed in 3993f83. npm run release:check PASS: 398/398 tests, zero failures/skips, exact 100/100/100/100 statements/lines/branches/functions over all 23 sources, no exclusions or lowered thresholds, 203 documented declarations, strict typecheck/lint, zero duplication, identity and publish-attestation gates, zero production vulnerabilities, pack dry run and changelog check. PM-linked terminal-candidate regression PASS via pm test pm-rl-od32 --run --progress --only-last. npm run changelog:full regenerated the unchanged completed-release changelog. pm health --strict-exit --json exits zero with existing advisories already tracked in pm-rl-9uz4. Item remains in_progress for orchestrator verification; claim released at stop. No GitHub replies."
  "2026-10-11T04:57:17.127Z",codex-agent,"Inspecting the existing durable controller and bounded causal-LM path; this change will strengthen generation-step replay, expiring lease contention, and real-process crash/cancellation drills. External decision receipt recovery in PR #65 remains separate."
  "2026-10-11T05:02:35.400Z",codex-sol-review,"Read-only review by codex-sol-review for pm-rl-od32. Read pm context/search/list-open, pm get pm-rl-od32 and pm get pm-rl-apvf; reviewed index.ts, lm.ts, test/durable-loop.test.ts and test/lm-loop.test.ts. This is a static review of actively changing implementation, not final-head acceptance. Initial index.ts had the long identity-based lease; a later read includes controllerMutex/guard and the 60-second lease. Latest observed index.ts digest: 7be64575f3226821fee0ce3014ef3c19a1813cef8dc59dcba3a6393abe559b14. Named functions below remain the anchors as lines change.\n\nP1 - Capture the acquired token before releasing the acquisition mutex. In index.ts acquireControllerLease, releaseRecovery runs before launch-authority initialization and before the read that sets token. If controller A stalls there beyond expiry, B can replace the lease; A then reads B's token and its guard accepts B's authority. Capture and validate a nonempty token from A's acquired SDK record while still under the mutex; never refresh a controller's expected token from a later disk read. Keep launch-authority mutations under this same fencing discipline.\n\nP1 - Fence every mutation at its commit boundary, not only the entry check. Latest observed guard calls cover preparation, seed release, cancellation comment and terminal report, but executePendingGeneration still creates runs, appends notes, closes runs, publishes checkpoints, registers candidates, records refusals and promotes without guard. A holder displaced while paused at onPhase can resume those effects. Include promotion's in-lock read/check/write, and do not convert loop_lease_lost or lock contention into a permanent promotion refusal. Serialize takeover, renewal, publication and cleanup under one SDK mutex with fixed lock order, or use a sink-enforced token/epoch CAS. A standalone assertOwned followed by an awaited write has a check-to-use race. SDK lock release checks its token; the seed claim needs the same invocation-level fencing, especially when both controllers use the same PM author.\n\nP1 - Renewal must be atomic and crash recoverable. The new guard writes the lease directly with writeFile, which truncates before replacing the content. SIGKILL during renewal can leave empty/partial JSON; controllerExpiry becomes invalid and acquisition refuses even explicit takeover. Reuse the temporary-file publication pattern under the mutex and preserve the acquired token. expireDeadControllerMutex also rewrites an inode in place: test a crash between write/truncate and subsequent recovery. A phase mutex with a billion-second lifetime that refuses takeover of a live/unverifiable holder protects safety but prevents bounded recovery of a hung holder during its guarded operation; state that availability limit or move long computation outside the commit mutex and reject late results at publication.\n\nP1 - PM receipts alone cannot eliminate the effect-to-receipt window. In index.ts completeGenerationEvidence/executePendingGeneration, fitting and evaluation finish before checkpoint publication and Generation registration. A crash after compute or artifact publication but before the receipt reruns the work and remeasures wall_ms, potentially changing the wall-limit verdict. Use a stable per-generation/per-step input identity binding programme digest, trainer version, source checkpoint, collection digest and derived step configuration. Store immutable completed step results plus required metadata, then reference them in PM; reconcile a published result missing its PM receipt before executing again. A crash before durable result publication can still require repeating pure computation; do not claim exactly-once execution from PM receipts. Likewise, a crash after promotion's body update but before close currently leaves promoted=true that inspectCandidateVerdict accepts as complete. Recovery should finish the recorded promotion outcome/close without spending approval twice, rather than treating that partially applied operation as a fresh promotion.\n\nP2 - Recovery and status currently execute completed LM work. inspectLmGeneration always calls lmCollectBatch, including before discovering no Run or an exhausted budget. verifyStoredLmGeneration calls executeLmStep, repeating fit/evaluation; executePendingGeneration recomputes them even when pending.item already exists. The new lm.ts restore helpers are useful but are not yet wired into those paths in the reviewed snapshot. Status/resume should validate receipt identities, checkpoint bytes, dataset/step linkage and exact event completeness without collect/train/evaluate calls. Validate duplicated, missing, reordered and foreign events when removing deterministic replay. Cache/restore the frozen base too: parseLmLoopConfig currently performs pretraining on every run/resume/status, before acquiring the execution lease.\n\nP2 - Synchronous CPU phases delay cancellation and renewal. lmCollectBatch, trainLmStep, evaluateLmStep and pretraining do not yield or consume AbortSignal; timer renewal and OS signal handlers cannot run during their work. Use a worker or bounded yielding chunks with deadline/cancellation checks; fence result adoption even after cancellation. Persist a fully completed result before acknowledging cancellation so resume can reuse it. Check cancellation before new work and after each separately persisted collect/train/evaluate phase; train/evaluate callbacks currently both occur after the combined candidate is registered.\n\nMissing evidence in test/durable-loop.test.ts and test/lm-loop.test.ts: phase-hook exceptions execute finally and are not hard crashes inside effect/receipt writes; existing takeover drills kill the old holder without letting it continue after replacement. Add separate counters proving zero completed collect/train/evaluate calls on status/resume; SIGKILL around result publication, PM receipt writes and promotion body/close; expired live-holder takeover followed by old-holder continuation; same-author stale cleanup; acquisition-token capture race; truncated renewal recovery; and real cancellation during CPU work. Match resumed reports to an uninterrupted reference, including accounting and wall-limit policy, rather than only comparing repeated resumed reports.\n\nTests: no test commands run; static code/test review only. Only this review comment is authored; no claim/status/release/close changes, no source edits, no commits or pushes, no PR action, no changes to pm-rl-9nlg or external System One receipt logic. Open risks above remain for implementation and orchestrator verification. STOP."
  "2026-10-11T05:08:36.719Z",codex-agent,"Added immutable generation-step PM receipts, separate causal-LM fit and held-out evaluation, persisted frozen base weights for resume, finite controller leases with token fencing, and cancellation history. Review identified and fixed acquisition-token capture and atomic lease-renewal windows. Real-process drills now cover SIGKILL inside PM writes, simultaneous contenders, expired-holder continuation and SIGTERM at a collection boundary. Validation is in progress."
  "2026-10-11T05:20:37.208Z",codex-agent,"Direct real-process expiry fencing and SIGTERM cancellation drills passed (2/2), as did the existing four-boundary bandit crash/replay drill (1/1) and separate LM fit/evaluation restoration checks (1/1). Linked pm test execution remains limited by foreign-branch command trust for prior entries and the existing pm-rl-warf sandbox tracker collision for new tracker-creating tests; direct package gates are running independently."
  "2026-10-11T05:23:09.057Z",codex-sol-faults,"Focused fault-test scope: add test/continuation-faults.test.ts only; use a real disposable PM tracker and one tiny-LM loop paused first after train and then after evaluate. Sequentially corrupt and restore durable receipt envelopes, LM receipt identities and candidate correspondence, and completed collection evidence. No SDK mocks, source edits, existing test edits, item ownership changes, commits, or PR changes. Read full stored bodies with unbounded output budgets."
  "2026-10-11T05:27:22.519Z",codex-sol-faults,"Static test decisions: receipt envelope faults run through public status/resume; semantic LM payload faults recompute the public hashJson envelope digest before validation. Training tests use the pre-candidate train pause; evaluation tests use the post-registration evaluate pause. Real stored run annotations are removed or truncated and restored through PM SDK updates. Initial TypeScript build:test and focused ESLint pass. First execution identified a null receipt body escaping as an untyped error; retaining the regression assertion and leaving implementation changes to the orchestrator."
  "2026-10-11T05:30:20.162Z",codex-sol-faults,"Fixture corrections in test/continuation-faults.test.ts: use the real notes edit API to remove metric evidence or replace it with a shorter encoded segment; full-item annotation snapshots correctly reject edits to existing audit entries. Treat candidate IDs as SDK-resolved tracker IDs. The first run stopped at fixture setup assertions (21 tests: 17 passed, 4 failed including the parent); only the null JSON typed-refusal failure was a controller finding. Corrected focused run is in progress. Exact command: node --test test/continuation-faults.test.ts. No source or existing test files changed by this work."
  "2026-10-11T05:30:25.639Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: in an isolated source copy, disabled only durableLoopStep's completed-receipt early return. The real SIGKILL LM resume regression failed (0/1; completed collect was repeated after mid-train), while the unchanged implementation's kill/race drills passed 2/2. The source worktree remained intact. The new expiry/cancellation drills also passed 2/2, proving safe takeover and a recorded boundary cancellation."
  "2026-10-11T05:31:03.368Z",codex-sol-faults,"Controller changed during the focused work: current index.ts now rejects non-object loop-step JSON before reading fields. The corrected run passes the null-envelope regression with the stable loop_step_drift refusal. This worker did not edit controller source. Current test file passes npm run build:test and focused ESLint; remaining runtime fault cases are still executing."
  "2026-10-11T05:34:31.868Z",codex-sol-faults,"Final focused results for test/continuation-faults.test.ts: node --test test/continuation-faults.test.ts passed 34/34 tests (33 sequential subtests plus the parent), 0 failed/cancelled/skipped/todo, duration 263540.515492 ms. npm run build:test passed. node_modules/.bin/eslint --config scripts/eslint.config.ts --max-warnings=0 test/continuation-faults.test.ts passed. Covered malformed/non-object envelopes; foreign format/key/input/state; absent or damaged result; rehashed LM fit/evaluation identity failures; valid alternate candidate checkpoint; candidate-versus-evaluation mismatch; real missing/truncated notes both before and after registration; restored evidence permitting exactly one promotion and idempotent resume without repeating collect/train/evaluate. One disposable tracker and one tiny-LM fixture; no PM SDK mocks. Earlier null-envelope controller failure is resolved by concurrent source changes and now passes. This worker edited only the new test file and these PM comments; no commits, pushes, source/existing-test/package edits, ownership transitions, PR changes, or other items touched. No unresolved controller issue observed by this focused suite; broader acceptance remains outside this task."
  "2026-10-11T05:40:37.398Z",codex-agent,"The real corruption suite passes 34/34 with one shared tiny-LM tracker. The controller now fences all effects through receipt publication, records promotion running before its effect, and reconciles a committed promotion body whose item close was interrupted without charging again. Completed local steps restore frozen base and numerical fit/evaluation evidence without replaying numerical work. Release thresholds remain unchanged at 100 percent in all four dimensions; full npm, Bun and clean Git identity validation are pending."
  "2026-10-11T05:52:12.763Z",codex-agent,"The current five SIGKILL boundaries including interrupted promotion close pass, together with expired live-holder fencing and SIGTERM cancellation: 3/3 focused parent tests. Existing force-takeover, atomic identity publication and lock-conflict checks pass 3/3. Receipt hardening now refuses rehashed non-object results. Native phase-lock owner identity also survives a kill before richer identity publication. Temp tracker initialization explicitly supplies its tracker path, following the SDK resolver precedence, so sandbox PM_PATH cannot redirect these drills into the test context tracker."
  "2026-10-11T06:00:17.794Z",codex-agent,"pm test pm-rl-od32 --run --only-last --progress now passes the real continuation-faults suite: 38/38 tests, zero failures, cancellations or skips, using explicit temp tracker paths and snapshot context. The direct focused feature matrix passed 43/43 tests; its mixed edit-time coverage was diagnostic only, not release evidence. Source commits 3360346 and 4c5aefe are frozen for full npm, Bun and clean HOME Git identity release gates at unchanged thresholds. The behavioral revert proof remains the isolated completed-step adoption revert that fails the SIGKILL regression with completed collect repeated after mid-train."
  "2026-10-11T06:01:04.990Z",codex-agent,"Full release checks rejected the fixture option path at build:test: the runtime init helper accepts PmClientOptions, so the correct explicit option is pmRoot. Corrected all three temp tracker helpers to cwd plus pmRoot without weakening TypeScript or coverage gates. Earlier direct and linked behavioral results remain recorded; full release validation is restarting after this compile fix."
  "2026-10-11T06:13:45.726Z",codex-agent,"A full-suite run exposed a timing-sensitive atomic-publication assertion; focused reproduction passes. Lease renewal introduces repeated atomic replacements and extra phase-mutex identity checks, so the regression must pin the original inode and verify the captured birth identity directly. Native file-fault drills will additionally verify dead-mutex inode races and the second controller-token check using real trackers and SDK lock operations. Handing the item claim to the focused CLI test worker while the orchestrator verifies the release diagnostics."
  "2026-10-11T06:16:42.161Z",codex-sol-native-faults,"Native fault test worker owns only test/controller-faults.test.ts and this item. Source remains frozen at e3a3303. Inspecting actual controller recovery, SDK lock records, and supported write observers for bounded numerical-bandit recovery and fencing drills; no SDK mocks or source edits."
  "2026-10-11T06:20:46.097Z",codex-sol-native-faults,"Added eight bounded native-controller tests using real SDK trackers and native lock publication: disappearance before open, successor token replacement, directory open failure with another main holder, two post-acquisition identity-storage failures, SDK successor takeover between guard checks, and completed collect/train receipt read failures. SDK write observers are activated through the supported test harness; OS probes delegate to native tooling. Initial typecheck and focused tests are running."
  "2026-10-11T06:22:38.130Z",codex-sol-native-faults,"Initial fixture validation found SDK read telemetry included in domain snapshots and a 30-second timeout under host contention. Snapshot assertions now select item TOON plus authoritative history, fixture cleanup restores cwd before deletion, and each drill remains bounded at 120 seconds. Typecheck and focused ESLint passed before these fixture refinements; full focused rerun is underway."
  "2026-10-11T06:25:22.451Z",codex-sol-native-faults,"Four native refusal/publication drills passed. The remaining assertions exposed tracker ID prefix normalization and brief-read body omission in the fixture, rather than controller failures. Evidence paths now use the actual SDK item ids with getHistoryPath/getItemPath, and receipt reads explicitly request standard depth with unbounded output. The guard-race test already observed loop_lease_lost and preserved all successor domain bytes before its corrected history-path assertion."
  "2026-10-11T06:27:03.389Z",codex-sol-native-faults,"All six native recovery/publication/fencing drills now pass. An isolated scratch source copy with only the open-inode token recheck removed produced the intended replacement-test assertion failure (1 test, 0 passes, 1 failure). The source worktree remains unchanged. Completed-receipt drills allow normal seed claim metadata/history churn but require identical receipt, run, candidate, and other domain bytes plus unchanged seed programme/status/ownership after cleanup."
  "2026-10-11T06:29:12.564Z",codex-sol-native-faults,"Completed collect/train storage replaced by real directories produced SDK read errors that propagated unchanged through resume. Final fixture assertions isolate the permitted seed claim timestamp/history changes and check unchanged seed body/status/assignee. Each drill now repairs the original receipt and proves one promotion, unchanged sample budget, and byte-identical reuse of the completed record. Final direct tests, typecheck, focused lint, and the second-guard isolated revert proof are running."
  "2026-10-11T06:30:10.702Z",codex-sol-native-faults,"Both isolated scratch revert proofs are now confirmed: removing the open-inode token recheck makes the successor-phase test miss its expected refusal; removing the second main-token guard check makes the guard-race test detect a rewritten successor lease. Each selected run executed 1 test with 0 passes and 1 intended assertion failure. Scratch copies were cleaned and index.ts was never edited. Final npm run build:test and focused ESLint both pass."
  "2026-10-11T06:32:07.241Z",codex-sol-native-faults,"Final direct node --test test/controller-faults.test.ts passed 8/8 with 0 failures, skips, or cancellations. npm run build:test and node_modules/.bin/eslint --config scripts/eslint.config.ts --max-warnings=0 test/controller-faults.test.ts passed. Real SDK boundaries: initialized trackers, native acquireLock records, harness onWrite observers, real successor acquisition/claim, delegated OS birth probes, and actual directory/read faults; no mocked SDK methods or return values. Permission-denied file modes and invalid-TOON parser cases were not separately exercised. Coverage manifest and full release gates remain with the orchestrator."
  "2026-10-11T06:33:50.549Z",codex-sol-native-faults,"Linked execution PM_AUTHOR=codex-sol-native-faults pm test pm-rl-od32 --run --only-last --progress passed the selected node --test test/controller-faults.test.ts command: 8 tests, 8 passes, 0 failures, cancellations, or test skips; exit 0. Effective contexts were none and snapshot with timeout_seconds=900. Automatic test-result tracking is disabled, so this sanitized comment records the receipt. Both targeted scratch revert assertions failed as intended. Work is ready for orchestrator inspection, coverage-manifest inclusion, and final gates; releasing without closing."
